  "description": "HALHOU crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C88 H128 Cu8 Gd4 N8 O32 4+,4(Cl1 O4 1-),16(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu3 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu4 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Cu5 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu6 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu7 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu8 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.167-3.945 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.52-111.45°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd4Cu8(OH)8(hep)8(O2CiPr)8](ClO4)4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
